=================
nwu.edu.critique
=================
* Edu -- Northwestern U. -- Critique

Summary: This is a critique of the policies of Northwestern U.'s
Academic Computing and Network Services (ACNS) organization. The
intellectual freedom policy is very good. Due-process policy is
fatally flawed: ACNS improperly claims authority to judge alleged
offensives and impose summary punishments on students. This
contradicts explicit University policy (and the principles of academic
freedom). The privacy policy is better than most, but it is
confusingly expressed.  Northwestern U. general policy also requires
that students be given a voice in creating policy that affects them. I
don't know how (or if) students participated in the creation of these
policies.


