A critique of policies at the University of South Florida.  The
policies seem to try to authoritize illegal searches and summary
punishment. They would punish anyone who posted to
alt.sexual-abuse.recovery under a pseudonym. Indeed they are so vague,
that they prohibit all computer use. There is no sign that they were
created with user participation or with regard to academic freedom.


